# nr-office-comrs-platform: the Win32 and process layer of mixdog-office-com (src/platform/). Applied by the wave's wiring.
# Nothing here is a protocol method or a service: no SERVICE_PENDING change.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod identity;` (the module list) add:
    pub mod platform;
(`mod cleanup;`, `mod oneshot;`, `mod scripts;`, `mod session;` stay as they are. The module is public: tests/platform.rs and
platform_live.rs, and the later host tasks, use `mixdog_office_com::platform::{Platform, WindowsPlatform, FakePlatform, ...}`.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml
After the `[dependencies]` table, add the Windows-only dependency (windows 0.62.2 is already in Cargo.lock; every feature below
is a feature of that version; Win32_Security and Win32_System_IO are needed because CreateFileW/CreateEventW and
ReadFile/WriteFile carry those types in their signatures):

    [target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]
    windows = { version = "0.62.2", features = [
      "Win32_Foundation",
      "Win32_Globalization",
      "Win32_Graphics",
      "Win32_Graphics_GdiPlus",
      "Win32_Security",
      "Win32_Storage_FileSystem",
      "Win32_System_Com",
      "Win32_System_Diagnostics_ToolHelp",
      "Win32_System_IO",
      "Win32_System_Threading",
      "Win32_UI_WindowsAndMessaging",
    ] }

Cargo.toml has `autotests = false`, so the two test files are registered next to the existing `[[test]]` tables:

    [[test]]
    name = "platform"
    path = "tests/platform.rs"

    [[test]]
    name = "platform_live"
    path = "tests/platform_live.rs"

(The tests need no new dev-dependency: tokio's rt/macros/process/io-util, mixdog-rt, mixdog-testkit and the crate's own
`test-support` self-dev-dependency are already there. `FakePlatform` is compiled under `any(test, feature = "test-support")`.)
If the dispatch task's fragment also adds a `[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies] windows = ...` table, merge the two feature
lists into one entry (the union).

## native/core/Cargo.lock
The `mixdog-office-com` package gains the dependency "windows 0.62.2" (written `"windows"` if it is the only `windows` the
resolver lists for that package; keep the list sorted). `windows` and its `windows-core`, `windows-result`, `windows-strings`,
`windows-link`, `windows-implement`, `windows-interface` 0.62-line crates are already in the lock through mixdog-secure-desktop,
so nothing is added from the registry. Regenerate offline: `cargo metadata --offline --manifest-path native/core/Cargo.toml`.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Regenerate the hakari section if the lead's flow does so: this crate now unifies windows 0.62.2 with the features above
(Win32_System_Com, Win32_Graphics_GdiPlus, Win32_System_Diagnostics_ToolHelp are the ones no other member lists).

## The consumers (later tasks)
The host's STA thread builds one `WindowsPlatform::new()?` (it owns the wait event; create it on the thread that uses it) and
passes `&dyn Platform` to the session code; unit tests of that code pass `FakePlatform`. Interface summary:
`Platform::{try_get_running_file -> Option<RunningObject> (downcast::<windows::core::IUnknown>()), register_excel_instances,
process_id_for_window, foreground_window, hide_visible_windows_for_process, visible_window_count_for_process,
visible_window_descriptions_for_process, restore_foreground_window, find_window_by_class_and_title, activate_window,
hide_window, window_visible, process_ids_by_name, office_process_ids, excel_process_ids, process_start_ticks, process_exists,
wait_for_exit, kill_process, installed, installed_office_fonts -> FontSet, open_exclusive -> Box<dyn ExclusiveStream>,
file_appears_open, temp_dir, new_guid_n, sleep, now}`, and the pure helpers `normalize_path`, `office_process_name`,
`ticks_from_filetime`, `guid_text_n`. The DPI repair's exclusive open is `open_exclusive` (CreateFileW, share mode 0; the stream
implements Read + Write + Seek).
